# November 28, 2026: Carnegie libraries of Florida: a batch of the pass the owner asked for to put the buildings Andrew
# Carnegie paid for on the map. No Florida Carnegie library was on the Atlas before, and none of these pins has another
# Atlas place within 600 metres.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's list of Carnegie libraries in Florida and its articles; National Register
# records and nominations (the Park Service: Bradenton, Jacksonville, St. Petersburg's Mirror Lake library, Tampa, FAMU,
# the Old Fessenden Academy district); the Manatee County Clerk's and the Palmetto Historical Park's own pages; the Tampa-
# Hillsborough County library's West Tampa page; FAMU's Black Archives visiting page; the Alachua County Library District's
# history; the St Pete Catalyst; the University of North Florida's historic architecture photographs.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for street addresses, OpenStreetMap points for named buildings, Wikipedia points where neither
# answered; every pin looked at on the aerial.
